---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="0002. License governance content under CC BY-SA 4.0 | Macro Evidence"
  description="Governance decision 0002: License governance content under CC BY-SA 4.0. Status: Superseded."
>
  <PageIntro
    kicker="Governance decision"
    title="0002. License governance content under CC BY-SA 4.0"
    lead="Governance decision 0002 of the Macro Evidence Governance decision series."
  />

  <section class="section policy-page">
    <div class="site-container reading policy-reading-wide">
      <article class="policy-text">
        <p class="policy-status">
          <strong>Status:</strong>&#32;Superseded<br />&#32;<strong
            >Superseded by:</strong
          >&#32;<a
            href="/governance/decisions/0010-preserve-cc-by-sa-default-with-explicit-legal-form-exceptions"
            >decision 0010</a
          >
        </p>
        <h2 id="context">Context</h2>
        <p>
          The&#32;<code>macro-evidence/governance</code>&#32;repository contains
          Macro Evidence's public organizational governance, documentation
          standards, trademark policy, and cross-cutting decision records.
        </p>
        <p>
          The repository has been published under Creative Commons Attribution
          4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), which permits reuse and adaptation,
          including commercial use, subject to its attribution and other license
          conditions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Macro Evidence subsequently reviewed whether its governance corpus
          should remain maximally permissive or operate as a reciprocal
          open-content commons. The review considered current repository
          composition, contribution history, third-party provenance, downstream
          reuse, licensing simplicity, and the long-term consequences of
          ShareAlike.
        </p>
        <p>
          The repository contains governance and documentation material rather
          than software code. The repository history reviewed for this decision
          did not identify external substantive contributions or incorporated
          third-party governance material requiring separate relicensing
          permission.
        </p>
        <p>
          Existing CC BY 4.0 grants remain valid under their terms. This
          decision does not revoke or retroactively replace those grants.
        </p>
        <h2 id="decision">Decision</h2>
        <p>
          Beginning with implementation of this decision, publish the maintained
          macro-evidence/governance repository and future revisions under
          Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA
          4.0).
        </p>
        <p>
          Macro Evidence adopts reciprocal openness for this governance corpus:
          the material remains available for use, redistribution, adaptation,
          and commercial reuse, while adaptations that are shared must comply
          with the ShareAlike requirements of CC BY-SA 4.0 or an applicable
          compatible license.
        </p>
        <p>
          The repository's committed&#32;<code>LICENSE</code>&#32;remains the
          canonical license text for the current repository state.
        </p>
        <p>
          This decision applies only to&#32;<code
            >macro-evidence/governance</code
          >. It does not change the licenses of&#32;<code
            >macro-evidence/.github</code
          >,&#32;<code>macro-evidence/website</code>,&#32;<code
            >macro-evidence/macro-data-observatory</code
          >, data obtained or produced through Macro Data Observatory, or Macro
          Evidence's trademarks and brand identity. Those rights and
          repositories remain governed by their own applicable policies and
          licenses unless separately reconsidered.
        </p>
        <h2 id="consequences">Consequences</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The governance repository moves from CC BY 4.0 to CC BY-SA 4.0 for
            its current and future releases.
          </li>
          <li>
            Shared adaptations of material governed by the new license are
            subject to ShareAlike requirements.
          </li>
          <li>Commercial use remains permitted under CC BY-SA 4.0.</li>
          <li>
            Downstream users have less relicensing flexibility than under CC BY
            4.0.
          </li>
          <li>
            Historical material already made available under CC BY 4.0 remains
            usable under those previously granted terms.
          </li>
          <li>
            Future repository contributions made under the repository's
            licensing terms enter a reciprocal open-content environment unless
            separate terms apply.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>README.md</code>&#32;and&#32;<code>TRADEMARKS.md</code
            >&#32;are synchronized with the new repository license.
          </li>
          <li>
            The&#32;<code>.github</code>, website, MDO, data, and trademark
            licensing questions remain separate and require their own evidence
            and decisions.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <div class="reference-links">
        <a class="text-link" href="/governance/decisions">
          All Governance decisions →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
